  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">In an attempt to "decipher" the non-verbal background sounds of Princess Dianas funeral, Kemplin fed a recording through a computers voice recognition program. Sounds of horses hooves, applause, and the half-muffled bell clappers are transformed into a poem that unexpectedly resonates with the emotions and substance of the actual funeral. Printed Matter.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Computer generated poem, using the background noises of the funeral of Diana, Princess of Wales including the sound of the bells of Westminster Abbey, with their clappers half-muffled, and the muted applause of the crowds"--Cover.</subfield>
